Now only 1 line lacking terminal because `splitSentenceLine` split after `”` due prepared replace `”(?=又说)`? Wait line `而《周礼》说：“祀天则旅祭上帝。”又说：“祀地则旅祭四望。”` prepared should split after first `”` before `又说` into two lines:
1 `而《周礼》说：“祀天则旅祭上帝。”`
2 `又说：“祀地则旅祭四望。”`
Then map should append `。` to both because ends with `”`. But validation says line 441 is first line without terminal. Why didn't append? In normalize, condition `if (/[。！？；：]$/.test(sentence.trim())) return sentence; else append.` It should append. But the sentence ends with `”`, regex false, so append. Unless `splitSentenceLine` returns first piece with trailing newline? It slices from prepared with inserted newline: `prepared = line.replace(/”(?=又说)/g, "”\n")`. The loop sees char `”`, decrements quoteDepth to 0, then next char is newline, no split. At end, `start` after? It only splits at punctuation; period inside quote depth1 not split. After closing quote, no terminal. At the end, start is 0 and pushes entire prepared string, not two pieces. Then returns one string containing `\n`. Ah the inserted newline remains within piece. Then later `.map` sees sentence containing newline and ending `”`, appends `。` at end of second part only. First line inside string remains without punctuation. Need handle inserted newline by split prepared on `\n` before scanner, or scanner should when char newline and quoteDepth0 push slice and start next. Easiest: `const prepared = line.replace(...).split("\n")`; then process each. But function currently one string. We can modify:
```
const splitSentenceLine = (line) => line.replace(...).split("\n").flatMap(part => { scanner on part })
```
Or in scanner when char === "\n" and quoteDepth===0 push slice and start index+1. Add condition. Simpler:
```
if (quoteDepth ===0 && (terminals.includes(char) || char==="\n")) { push slice; start=index+1; }
```
But if char is newline, slice includes maybe terminal before? In first part ends `”`; push it. Then map appends `。`. Good. Do that.
