+test

Why newline condition didn't work? Let's inspect function code. Maybe `prepared` line replace uses straight double quote? We used `”` curly in regex and string. It should. The scanner sees newline char after `”`, quoteDepth0, pushes slice including newline? At index of newline, `prepared.slice(start,index+1)` includes newline, then map sees `sentence.trim()` ends `”`, appends `。` to end after newline? Actually sentence string ends with newline, `${sentence}。` yields:
`而...”\n。`
Then split by `\n` later? normalize returns `.join("\n")`, so line1 no punctuation and line2 `。`. That explains. Need trim sentence before appending or push slice without newline. In scanner when char newline, push `prepared.slice(start,index)` (excluding newline), start=index+1. For punctuation, include char. So condition separate:
```
if quoteDepth===0 && terminals.includes(char) push slice incl char
else if quoteDepth===0 && char==="\n" push slice start index; start=index+1
```
Patch.
