+test

Now only 16 terminal issues, all ending with `）`, `】`, `”`. Our normalizeSentence only accepts closing mark if preceded by terminal. But some lines end with `。”` where previous char is `。`? Wait `《诗经》说：“无德不报，无言不酬。”` ends with `”`, previous char `。`? The string ends `酬。”`, so previous char before `”` is `。`. Our regex `/([。！？；])([”』」）】])$/` should match. Why validation says lacking? Because validation regex only `/[。！？；：]$/`, not closing marks. Ah, `validateOutputs` still only checks line ends with terminal punctuation, not closing marks. It doesn't use normalizeSentence acceptance. We need update validation to accept lines ending with closing mark preceded by terminal. Also for `）` and `】` same. Lines like `（卷七终...。）` ends with `）` preceded by `。`, should accept. So patch validation:
```
if (/[。！？；：]$/.test(line) || /([。！？；])([”』」）】])$/.test(line)) continue;
```
Then no issues. Multi-sentence lines should be reduced. Let's patch.
codex
